  "title": "Prove global funding bounds for arbitrary helper dependencies with retained original targets and fixed P104 operations",
  "body": "## Exact result\n\nOn exact #7481, helper relations surjective onto any retained original-coordinate subset cannot improve the complete signed moment by deleting only identically zero MOVEs, for every0<=kappa<=1/4. Cross-group, nonlinear and operator-valued preparation are covered under that surjectivity and independence from mains. Preparation and cleanup are free in this upper bound. Earlier coordinate and matching-boundary subspace theorems are retained.\n\n## Why it holds and how to reproduce\n\nFresh source replay gives468 helper-only rows,rank463 and five exact dependencies. Their row spaces decompose into442 singletons plus11/5/5/5 blocks. All2140 local subsets are checked;31 dependent subsets satisfy6*minimum_linear_basis_price>=11*paid_rank_sum. Independent prefix ranks, a prime minor, exact relations and a block Laplace argument handle shared columns. The full17-call invoice is rebuilt. This extends #7307 predicates to fully charged input restrictions.\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/p104-all-helper-zeroing-bound\n```\n\nExpected PASS_HELPER_COORDINATE_AND_SUBSPACE_FUNDING_NO_GAIN. Normal/optimized and read-only Git-free export agree, including actual mutation controls.\n\n## Scope and credit\n\nCanonical base e54523517d0f03e58352e647c403a5af3e525a57; source #7481 head89eaa9d8cae37c1540de98f2d29a3abaabb96a2b. No newkappa; five foundations retained. Changed native operations, main-dependent preparations, new decoded targets and cache deletion of nonzero MOVEs remain outside scope. Prepared for Jerry Chen / @CubeJerry with substantial OpenAI assistance. Credit Clear1nsight #7481, Rohan Arun #7113, ToikY #7307 and original notices.\n\n[Full proposed description, proof and limitations](https://github.com/CubeJerry/integer-mult-bounds/blob/70d3eda833dde704522efad3ca155bc5aeb959b3/research/p104-all-helper-zeroing-bound/PR-DESCRIPTION.md).\n",
